As part of improving the Contextual Message component, we have optimized how the contextual message rules are checked, so that the messages keep showing even when many rules are set up.

Current Process
- Each contextual message rule is checked separately when a record page opens.
- When there are many rules, the system reaches its limit and stops.
- When this happens, none of the contextual messages are shown on the page.

New Process
- Each rule is now kept in its own file. The file holds the message and the list of records it applies to.
- Policy rule files start with CTX_POLICY_ and contact rule files start with CTX_CONTACT_, so it is easy to tell which page a rule belongs to.
- All the rule files for a page are read together in one step instead of one by one.
- The page then compares the rules with the record being viewed and shows the matching messages.
- To add, change or remove a rule, only its file needs to be updated. No code change is required.

This enhancement ensures that the component handles any number of rules without reaching system limits, improving reliability and making rules easier to maintain.

The changes are completed in the dev environment and testing is in progress.